    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nWhen doing multiple yanks with multicursor into unnamed plus or star registers, pasting only pastes what was yanked under the main cursor.  \nThe \" register and named registers work fine by joining the copied items with new line.  \nThus setting `:set clipboard=unnamedplus` defeats the purpose when using multicursor \n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open any file in nvim\n  ```\n  nvim --clean\n  :e foo.txt\n  ```\n2. Add cursors at multiple lines with `Q` or `<C-LeftMouse>`\n3. Yank the lines into any of plus or star unnamed registers (`\"+yy` or `\"*yy`)\n4. Clear cursors (exit multicursor session) `<C-l>`\n5. Put the yanked texts from the register (`\"+p` or `\"*p`) and find only the text under main cursor pasted\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe yanks should be joined (linewise) when the multicursor session ends for unnamed[plus] registers too as it does with \" and named registers\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nv0.13.0-dev-1531+g48864161cd\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nNA, vim doesn't have multicursor\n\n### Operating system/version\n\narchlinux 7.1.11-arch1-1\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nkitty 0.48.2\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-kitty\n\n### Installation\n\nInstalled nightly version using bob",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
